  "motion": {
    "frames": 120,
    "note": "Airborne blade-winged dragon (the official art and dream-world art show it in the air, legs dangling, toes down; the menu icon shows it flying), so no plant: a slow hover driven by the arm-blades. 120 frames = 3.6 s = 2 slow strokes. The arms lift and fall (driver); the elbows, then the blade-wings and their outer halves follow a beat later each; the body rises a couple of px on each downstroke and drifts sideways once a loop; spine and head counter-nod a little; the dangling legs, then knees, then pointed feet swing a beat behind; the tail undulates down its length with a slower side sway, tail fins last."
